From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Tue, 7 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: skip the prefix ownership check on PS5/PS4 too.

create_dir() already skips its st_uid test under __PROSPERO__, with the note
"one user; its file systems do not keep unix owners". create_server_dir() makes
the same test against the prefix itself and was left unguarded, so it fires
whenever the prefix was not written by the running user.

On PS4 that is always: the prefix is pushed with tools/pw_prefix.py over the
console's FTP server, so every file in it belongs to that server's uid, and
chmod cannot change ownership. wineserver then called

    fatal_error( "%s is not owned by you\n", config_dir )

and fatal_error died writing to a stderr that goes nowhere, taking the title
with it as an uncatchable SIGSYS. The backtrace, symbolised against the module
bases, read create_server_dir -> fatal_error.

Guard it the same way as the first.
---
diff --git a/server/request.c b/server/request.c
index 81fe8f4ab8..ca91a38baf 100644
--- a/server/request.c
+++ b/server/request.c
@@ -1009,8 +1009,10 @@ static char *create_server_dir( int force )
         fatal_error( "open %s: %s\n", config_dir, strerror( errno ));
     if (fstat( config_dir_fd, &st ) == -1)
         fatal_error( "stat %s: %s\n", config_dir, strerror( errno ));
+#ifndef __PROSPERO__  /* one user; its file systems do not keep unix owners */
     if (st.st_uid != getuid())
         fatal_error( "%s is not owned by you\n", config_dir );
+#endif
 
     /* create the base directory if needed */
 
